"text": "**The gates:** - the harness crate's own unit tests, now built with the feature (gate 1); - the new check, per package — the build selection that read red (gate 2); - the whole of blitz-tests and of seven_guis per package (gates 3, 4): both now compile blitz-paint's widget pass where   they did not, so every pixel test and every process check is re-read under the moved feature set; - three probes read once, never a source mutation: the feature now reaches the harness, the driver and seven_guis   (gate 5, red on the untouched tree by construction — its red reading is P5's baseline); the stand graph holds no   platform adapter (gate 6, a re-read of architecture · established-decisions/decision/driver-builds-no-platform-adapter,   a standing guard no step moves, so it takes no control); the lock moves by one line (gate 7, reading no line on the   untouched tree); - the pre-push gate (`fast`), the `audit` leg (the lock moves; security-plan ·   dependency-security/decision/local-audit-before-push), and `stand-repeat`, which takes `stand_canvas_shot` by its   `stand_` prefix and runs it three rounds per package (gates 8–10)."
},
{
"from": 110,
"to": 113,
"text": "**What no step changes:** no boot path or binary start (the stand's served table and boots are untouched; F2 A), no log site, span or field, no public doc comment (so no `doc` leg), no a11y leg file (so no `a11y` leg), no served task, so `host_log`, `mcp_log` and the cold-agent pipe are not run. There is no live leg and no headful self-verify on this project."
},
{
"from": 115,
"to": 116,
"text": "**Controls.** The check is red before the fix (step 3) and under the one-shot `gate.py control` of step 6; gate 5's red is its P5 baseline on the untouched tree; gate 7 reads no line there. No other new control."
},
{
"from": 118,
"to": 120,
"text": "The diff is not OS-sensitive: no `cfg` site is added or changed. The operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand because this chunk's verdict reads a CI run, as every chunk's does; CI's `test` leg (workspace) and `Stand checks repeated` (per package) are the two selections the check runs under there."
}
],
